@startuml
!include includes/report-style.iuml

start
:React route guard and role-aware controls;
:Protected action carries current target IDs;
:API checks active session and role;
:API checks project relation;
:Load target and lifecycle state;
:Recheck manager/access,\nlifecycle, and target inside transaction;
:Database constraints backstop the write;
if (All checks pass?) then (yes)
  :Commit write;
  :Invalidate affected queries;
else (no)
  :Return 401, 403, or 409;
  :Refresh affected data when stale;
endif
stop

note right
  Access control is layered:
  UI guard -> API authz -> transaction recheck -> DB constraints.
end note
@enduml
